--
libstdc++ 13's <format>: the four inline std::vformat overloads
(format:3784/3793/3802/3811) were dropped with "scope '__format' is
ambiguous" -- the class template __format::_Arg_store is declared in
namespace std::__format, defined outside it by a qualified name, and the
namespace is reopened afterwards; see test.desc (header-free, CORE).  That
is fixed.  Now __formatter_fp::format (format:1422) is dropped: the visitor
lambda of _Formatting_scanner::_M_format_arg is generic, and its body is
also type-checked speculatively with `int' for auto, which instantiates
format with an unresolved `_Type' (cpp14_generic_lambda_body_checked_with_
placeholder_type).  Round-163 audit: cpp20_format_header.  Pre-existing
(round-162 snapshot bin51).
